WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.220 line:17%
Two needs can show up during the same visit.

00:00:02.992 --> 00:00:05.650 line:17%
First, a caregiver asks what the audiogram means.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:08.990 line:17%
Explaining the result, the available options, and what happens

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:10.670 line:17%
next is informational counseling.

00:00:11.723 --> 00:00:14.570 line:17%
Then the caregiver says the diagnosis still feels overwhelming.

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:17.770 line:17%
Acknowledging that reaction and helping the family work through

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:19.750 line:17%
what it means is adjustment counseling.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:23.150 line:17%
The audiogram is the same, and the purpose of

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:24.350 line:17%
the exchange has changed.

00:00:25.594 --> 00:00:28.554 line:17%
Families also need enough information to make decisions on

00:00:28.554 --> 00:00:29.654 line:17%
their child's behalf.

00:00:30.354 --> 00:00:33.434 line:17%
An audiologist can compare the benefits and limitations of

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:36.114 line:17%
the options and explain a professional recommendation.

00:00:37.034 --> 00:00:40.314 line:17%
The family brings its priorities, including the communication routines

00:00:40.314 --> 00:00:41.254 line:17%
that matter to them.

00:00:42.054 --> 00:00:44.734 line:17%
Together they can use clinical evidence and those priorities

00:00:44.734 --> 00:00:46.314 line:17%
to identify a next step.

00:00:47.164 --> 00:00:50.004 line:17%
As families build knowledge and confidence, the clinician can

00:00:50.004 --> 00:00:52.524 line:17%
shift toward helping them advocate for the choices they

00:00:52.524 --> 00:00:53.164 line:17%
make.
